{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Shape.Checkpoint</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"neural_nets_lib","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Ocannl_tensor","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Shape","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Checkpoint","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[{"title":"Checkpoints (gh-ocannl-903)","href":"#checkpoints-(gh-ocannl-903)","children":[]}],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"","content":"<h4 id=\"checkpoints-(gh-ocannl-903)\"><a href=\"#checkpoints-(gh-ocannl-903)\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Checkpoints (gh-ocannl-903)</h4><p>The shape-inference half of <code>Tensor.checkpoint</code>: use that. A checkpoint snapshots the open frontier -- this module's and <code>Row</code>'s module-level session state (persistent values, captured as pointers), and the mutable fields of the shapes and steps of the active update steps and of every live capture reference -- and a rewind puts them back and discards what the window created.</p><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-label\"><a href=\"#val-label\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> label : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-is_closure\"><a href=\"#val-is_closure\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> is_closure : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.bool</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-refusal\"><a href=\"#val-refusal\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> refusal : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.option</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Why the checkpoint can no longer be rewound to: a closure since it was taken, a rewind past it (or to the last closure, or a reset), a raising committed-state read of a shape open at the checkpoint, or a shape older than it outside its frontier. <code>None</code> when it can be. Checked before a rewind writes anything.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-categories\"><a href=\"#val-categories\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> categories : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The restore categories <a href=\"#val-rewind\"><code>rewind</code></a> can be told to <code>omit</code>: negative controls only.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-rewind\"><a href=\"#val-rewind\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> rewind : <span><span class=\"optlabel\">?omit</span>:<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"label\">provenance</span>:<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Discards the window's shapes, update steps and the capture references it made and touched (with <code>provenance</code>); restores the frontier's objects and the module-level state; clears the taint. The caller checks <a href=\"#val-refusal\"><code>refusal</code></a> first.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-differences\"><a href=\"#val-differences\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> differences : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The components of the session that differ from the checkpoint, by name: a diagnostic.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-sizes\"><a href=\"#val-sizes\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> sizes : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span>(<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string * <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.int)</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The open frontier's sizes at the checkpoint: a diagnostic.</p></div></div>"}